# /public/build is deliberately TRACKED. The deploy target is cPanel shared hosting with no
# Node runtime, so the server cannot run `npm run build` — the compiled CSS/JS has to arrive
# with the clone or the site serves unstyled HTML. Vite empties this directory on every build
# (outDir is inside the project root, so emptyOutDir defaults on), so the hashed filenames
# are replaced rather than accumulated, and the raw files delta-compress between versions
# in a way a gzipped build archive would not. Run `npm run build` before committing a change
# to anything under resources/css or resources/js.
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
